<title>FRANCE: Cerus requotes at 138.00 francs.</title>
<headline>Cerus requotes at 138.00 francs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French holding company Cerus requoted at 1000 GMT at a price of 138 francs after being suspended limit down twice after CGIP denied reports it was planning a public offer for Cerus.</p>
<p>Cerus, which owns 28 percent of car parts maker Valeo, is the French holding company of Italian businessman Carlo De Benedetti who resigned last week as chairman of Olivetti.</p>
<p>At 1005 the share was trading at 130.00 Ffr, down 5.80.</p>
<p>--  Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
